vred_iback1 is a test version of vred that applies a pseudo-rescor to an amp during reductions,
  but based locally on that instance of the amp alone.
 
 It may do well to remove unnatural "sky" lines that are angled over the
  detector (e.g. local lamps, LEDs, etc that are not following the same
  optical path as the real sky lines). ... the effect is you can see them
  in the cleaned_image, where they are over- then under- subtracted at one
  end of the amp and as you move to the other end (top to bottom), they flip
  to under- then over- subtracted.

  A consequence though, is that you can loose lines that are real and cover
  much of the amp (e.g. extended objects, planetary nebulae, etc)

